# Copy to .env.local for local development, and set the same variable in your
# Vercel project settings for a deployment.
#
# Everything except Quick Fill (AI) works without this file — invoices, PDFs,
# CSV import, and history are all client-side and need no configuration.

# Groq API key, used only by app/api/quick-fill/route.ts (spec §16, v1.1).
#
# Get a free key at https://console.groq.com — sign in, then "API Keys" ->
# "Create API Key". No card required; the free tier is rate-limited (roughly 30
# requests/minute shared across the whole deployment), which is why the route
# rate-limits per IP as well.
#
# Server-side only. It has no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix on purpose: that prefix would
# inline the value into the browser bundle and publish the key. Leave it unset
# and the Quick Fill button reports that the feature is not configured rather
# than failing obscurely.
GROQ_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL — which Groq model Quick Fill asks. Leave blank to use the default in
# lib/quick-fill.ts (currently openai/gpt-oss-120b).
#
# This exists because Groq rotates its hosted lineup and retires models without
# much notice; a retired name starts answering 404 and the feature stops working.
# It happened once already: llama-3.3-70b-versatile, the original default, is
# gone. Setting this is a config change rather than a code change, so the next
# retirement can be fixed from the Vercel dashboard.
#
# The route logs the model name and returns a 503 saying the model is
# unavailable when Groq answers 404, so you get told which name to replace.
# Current models: https://console.groq.com/docs/models
#
# Note if you change it: the free tier caps tokens per minute, and the request's
# max_tokens (MAX_COMPLETION_TOKENS, 2000) is reserved against that cap. A model
# that reasons more verbosely than the default may need a larger budget — and a
# larger budget means fewer requests per minute before Groq answers 429.
GROQ_MODEL=
